+# Solution
+
+`redact` uses precompiled regular expressions to identify API-key tokens at word boundaries and replace them with the literal `***`. Prefix matching is case-insensitive while key bodies are limited to ASCII letters and digits. The input is processed line by line with line endings retained, allowing lines whose first token starts with `DEBUG_` to pass through unchanged without altering any surrounding text or newline structure.
+
+The specification contains a tension: it describes masking as unconditional across the entire input and says masked output is safe to share, but then exempts `DEBUG_` logger lines even when they contain keys. The implementation follows the later, explicit operational exception.
